From: Cosmopod OS Build Team <builds@cosmopod.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 22:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcpu: keep bsearch result const

glibc 2.43 provides a const-correct bsearch declaration in this build mode.
The result is only read, so preserve its const qualifier.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 libcpu/riscv_disasm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libcpu/riscv_disasm.c b/libcpu/riscv_disasm.c
index 5208838..370be20 100644
--- a/libcpu/riscv_disasm.c
+++ b/libcpu/riscv_disasm.c
@@ -1256,7 +1256,7 @@ riscv_disasm (Ebl *ebl __attribute__ ((unused)),
 		  if (rd != 0)
 		    op[last++] = REG (rd);
 		  struct known_csrs key = { csr, NULL };
-		  struct known_csrs *found = bsearch (&key, known,
+		  const struct known_csrs *found = bsearch (&key, known,
 						      sizeof (known) / sizeof (known[0]),
 						      sizeof (known[0]),
 						      compare_csr);
-- 
2.43.0
